Q: How to enable ipv6 for WSL while keeping docker-ce intact? A: <p>Edit <code>/etc/docker/daemon.json</code> and add <code>&quot;userland-proxy&quot;: false</code> to the top level. Either restart WSL from host  <code>wsl.exe --shutdown</code> or restart Docker in WSL using <code>sudo service docker restart</code> .</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>{
    &quot;userland-proxy&quot;: false
}
</code></pre>
<p>According to <a href="https://github.com/moby/moby/issues/48056#issuecomment-2315995230" rel="nofollow noreferrer">this GitHub comment</a>, when enabling mirrored mode, the NAT rules applied by docker-proxy no longer apply correctly and interfere with the networking, making docker containers unavailable from the host.</p>
